# A sort under a comparator copies the values of the list out into a scratch list that the comparator never sees, and back. Each of the two run-copies asks the program's list for its kind and its length in every build;
# of the scratch list the library vouches: it was born with boxed storage and is long enough. Under `--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges` its kind is held too: boxed words are stored into it, or read out of it, whatever it is.
# And the program's list may keep storage for int32s: what goes back into that is an int32.
